From: Uke contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep rollback-off kernel updates on alternating inactive slots

Use an explicitly unapproved rotating checkpoint instead of replacing current A.
Preserve accepted kernel recovery components before reusing its physical slot,
keep approval separate from bootloader retention, and retain existing inactive
write, firmware, GPT, UFS, charge, locking and readback boundaries.

